    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d36">

                <pb facs="0088" n="78" xml:id="pg78"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Adams.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 808.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-01-12"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 12, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your despatch of the 3d of December last
                    (No. 547) has been received, together with the copy of the correspondence which,
                    at that date, had taken place between yourself and Earl Russell on the subject
                    of the Rappahannock. I have the pleasure of informing you that not only your
                    proceedings mentioned in the despatch, but also the views and suggestions
                    therein contained, in regard to a just treatment of the case of the
                    Rappahannock, and kindred subjects, are approved by the President.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles F. Adams</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
